## Task 3 — Stale-while-revalidate for both discovery caches ✅

Added a shared, framework-agnostic `StaleWhileRevalidateCache<T>` primitive in `@openthrottle/openthrottle-agentic-utils` (`src/utils/cache/stale-while-revalidate.ts`, exported `@public`) and wired both services onto it, replacing their bespoke TTL/inFlight logic:

**Primitive semantics** — `get(load, { softTtlMs, hardTtlMs }, forceRefresh?)`:
- within soft TTL → return fresh snapshot;
- past soft, within hard → return last-good snapshot **synchronously** + kick a single coalesced background refresh (no block);
- no snapshot OR past hard TTL → block on a scan (coalesced with any in-flight);
- at most one scan (blocking or background) ever in flight;
- a failed background refresh is swallowed → last-good snapshot survives, next call retries (cache never poisoned);
- `hardTtlMs` clamped up to `softTtlMs`; clock injectable (defaults to `() => Date.now()` so fake timers installed after construction still take effect).

**Config / env knobs**:
- Model: added `hardTtlMs` to `ModelDiscoveryConfig` + `LLM_DISCOVERY_HARD_TTL_MS` (default `DEFAULT_HARD_TTL_MULTIPLIER`=10× the soft `LLM_DISCOVERY_CACHE_TTL_MS`, clamped ≥ soft; collapses to 0 when caching disabled). Joi schema updated.
- Agent (server-local service, read from `process.env` at construction, documented in the class JSDoc): `AGENT_DISCOVERY_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 60_000) + `AGENT_DISCOVERY_HARD_TTL_MS` (default 600_000, clamped ≥ soft). Server `ConfigModule.forRoot` has no strict validationSchema, so these unknown vars don't affect boot.

**Tests**: primitive suite (9 tests — first-ever blocks, fresh within soft, stale-synchronous + exactly-one-background-refresh past soft, concurrent-stale coalescing, blocks past hard, failed-refresh keeps last-good, forceRefresh, invalidate, concurrent first-ever coalescing). Model service +2 SWR tests (stale+bg past soft; blocks past hard) and 4 config tests (hard-TTL default/explicit/clamp/collapse-to-0). Agent service tests reworked for SWR (stale+bg past soft, blocks past hard, `AGENT_DISCOVERY_CACHE_TTL_MS` shortens the fresh window).

**Validation**: agentic-utils 360 tests, model-discovery 23 tests, server 1215 tests all pass; lint + typecheck clean on all three projects. No GraphQL schema/resolver changes → no codegen.

Task 3 — Add updateProject + edit-loader GraphQL docs and run codegen

- New sidecar app/routes/projects.$projectId.edit.tsx.graphql:
  - query getProjectForEdit($id: ID!) → project { description, id, name, nxProjectName, updatedAt }
  - mutation updateProject($input: UpdateProjectInput!) → updateProject { description, id, name, nxProjectName, updatedAt }
  Verified against schema.gql: updateProject(input: UpdateProjectInput!): ProjectObject; UpdateProjectInput { id: ID!, name, description, nxProjectName }.
- Ran codegen-graphql: GetProjectForEditDocument + UpdateProjectDocument generated into app/__generated__/{gql,graphql}.ts. No applications/openthrottle-server/schema.gql drift (server unchanged, as expected).

