Task 2 — Updated ChatThread tests (packages/react-router-chat/src/components/__tests__/ChatThread.test.tsx).

Added a stateful `renderControllable` harness so a single mounted ChatThread survives message updates (refs carry over), then asserted the new triggers:
- new user message appended → scrolls once (smooth);
- assistant first token (pending/empty → non-empty body, same id) → scrolls exactly once (smooth);
- subsequent body growth on SAME assistant id → NO further scroll (call-count guard) — the core regression test;
- near-bottom guard: stubbed container geometry + dispatched a scroll event to mark "scrolled up", verified the first-response scroll is suppressed while a fresh user-send still scrolls.
Kept the existing empty-mount and first-paint(`auto`) guards.

Gotchas hit + fixed: (1) two ChatThreads in the DOM (outer beforeEach also renders one) → scoped the geometry query with `within(result.container)`; (2) react/no-multi-comp on the harness → added the repo-standard `eslint-disable-next-line react/no-multi-comp -- test-local` comment.

Validated: react-router-chat test 265 passed (was 261; +4), typecheck ✓, lint ✓.
